    </div>

    <h2>Fun Fact</h2>

    <p>
        Monroe was nearly kidnapped by British forces
        during the War of 1812. While riding in his
        carriage near Washington, D.C., he encountered
        British sailors who demanded he surrender.
        He refused, saying, "I have the confidence of
        my countrymen." His courage helped save him.
        This incident led to his later nickname
        "Monroe the Magnificent."
    </p>
    <p>Monroe also had the distinction of being the
    last president born before the American Revolution.
    His administration (1817–1825) is known as the
    "Era of Good Feelings" because, for the first
    time, there was no partisan rivalry between
    the major political parties at the national
    level.
