        <strong>Birth:</strong> March 15, 1767<br>
        <strong>Death:</strong> June 8, 1845
    </div>

    <h2>Fun Fact</h2>
    <p>
        Jackson carried two bullets in his chest from a
        duel in 1805. He had them removed after each
        shot was fired, but the wound never fully healed,
        leaving him in constant pain.
    </p>
    <blockquote>
        "I had the honor of meeting you in person last
        evening at the White House, where you were
        the guest of our President. There was no
        occasion for a more formal introduction, and
        I therefore make it without the ceremony."
    </blockquote>

    <p>Jackson was known to be incredibly tough and
    was often called "Old Hickory" by his soldiers
    because his men compared his toughness to
    hickory wood. He was the last president whose
    parents had died before he took office.</p>

