        <strong>Birth:</strong> December 5, 1782<br>
        <strong>Death:</strong> July 24, 1862
    </div>

    <h2>Fun Fact</h2>
    <p>
        Van Buren was the only president born after the
        Declaration of Independence and the only president
        who spoke English as a second language. He spoke
        Dutch with his parents. Born in 1782, he was the
        last president born in the Netherlands, a small
        town in Albany County, New York.
    </p>
    <p>
        He was also called "The Little Magician" by
        political opponents because of his short stature
        (he was 5'3" and weighed only 120 pounds).
        The nickname was originally a compliment to his
        political skill, but his enemies used it to
        suggest he was crafty.
    </p>

