    <h2>Fun Fact</h2>
    <p>Andrew Jackson was the first president to own enslaved people. He was also a duelist — Jackson fought over 100 duels and was the first president to <em>win</em> all of them. Before his presidency, Jackson killed Charles Dickinson in a duel over a dispute with Dickinson about Jackson's wife Rachel. The bullet entered Jackson's cheek and lodged near his heart, and he kept it embedded in his body for the rest of his life. He also famously had a pet raccoon named "Jack" that he took to the White House, where it caused havoc by tearing up his dinner before the dinner guests.</p>
