    <h2>Fun Fact</h2>
    <p>Martin Van Buren was the only U.S. president who <em>was not born a U.S. citizen</em> because he was born before the Declaration of Independence, in 1782, before the country existed. The nickname "Van Buren" (which he went by for most of his life) was a playful corruption of his own name "Buren." After his presidency, Van Buren ran for president again in 1848 as the Liberty Party candidate and received 10% of the popular vote — the most of any third-party presidential candidate in 1848. He was also the only president to speak Dutch as his first language.</p>
