    <p>William Henry Harrison holds the record for the <em>shortest presidency in American history</em> — just 31 days. Harrison died of pneumonia (or possibly typhoid) shortly after delivering the longest inaugural address in history (nearly two hours in freezing weather without a coat) during his inauguration on March 4, 1841. Before becoming president, Harrison was known as "Old Tippecanoe" after his victory at the Battle of Tippecanoe. Interestingly, Harrison was the last president to have been born before the United States declared independence, and the only president who had never served in the civilian government before assuming the presidency.</p>
